filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-10-16: in a WebAssembly
build a download or an upload ends at once, as one the converter is not
allowed to make (Common/Network/FileTransporter/src/FileTransporter_private.h).

x2t fetches what a document names elsewhere with core's CFileDownloader: a
.docx's linked picture (TargetMode="External", CMediaManager::WriteImage),
an HTML page's <img> or style sheet (HtmlFile2), a picture of a pptx, an
xlsx, a ppt or a PDF. CFileTransporter_private starts a thread for it
(CBaseThread::Start) and TransferSync waits while the thread runs, in a
loop of NSThreads::Sleep(10). WebAssembly - the page's build and the
server's - has no threads: pthread_create fails, Start does not look, the
transfer stays "running" with no thread to end it, and the loop never
ends. In the server build nanosleep is emscripten's busy wait on the
clock, so the module spun at full speed until the host's deadline.

Measured (2026-10-16, a .docx whose one picture is linked from
http://127.0.0.1:9/, an HTML page with an <img> and one with a <link
rel="stylesheet"> on that address): the server build under wazero did not
finish in 200 s (into the editor's format; the same .docx without the
picture 13 ms), the page's x2t in Node not in 40 s (46 ms without);
counted with a stand-in for WASI's clock_time_get, 3,000,000 calls in half
a second, every one from CFileDownloader::DownloadSync -> NSThreads::Sleep
-> nanosleep -> emscripten_get_now (the stacks of a build with names).

Here, under __EMSCRIPTEN__, the transporter's Start runs the transfer on
the caller's thread, and ThreadProc takes the branch it takes when the
process environment says allowNetworkRequest is false: nothing is fetched,
the file is not downloaded (a partial one is removed), the callback hears
1, IsRunned() is false when Start returns. Every caller already handles a
download that failed: a linked picture is left out (WriteImage gets no
file), an HTML page's picture stays a link to its address with its alt
text, a style sheet is not read - what a Document Server without a network
does (its own x2t, run with docker's --network none: the same .docx to PDF
in 1.1 s, its thumbnail the same picture as the .docx without the link; an
HTML page with a picture elsewhere to docx, the same document.xml as this
build's). After: 13 ms on the server,
49 ms in Node, no clock_time_get call; the documents without such
addresses come out as before.

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

